# Symfony GraphQL SDK

This package includes the portable PHP GraphQL SDK and a Symfony bundle. Models,
selection-specific variables, result validation and raw/flat/grouped calls come
from the PHP generator. Enable the bundle:

```php
// config/bundles.php
return [__NAMESPACE__\__BUNDLE__::class => ['all' => true]];
```

```yaml
# config/packages/graphql.yaml
__ALIAS__:
  endpoint: '%env(GRAPHQL_ENDPOINT)%'
  headers:
    Authorization: 'Bearer %env(GRAPHQL_TOKEN)%'
  timeout: 30.0
  http_client: http_client
```

Autowire `__SDK__\Client`. A named scoped HttpClient service can replace
`http_client`. Calls preserve GraphQL errors and partial data; use
`$response->requireData()` when errors should throw. No mutation retries or
redirects are added by this bundle. Your supplied HTTP client may have its own
retry policy; configure it appropriately for mutations.

Runtime scalar callbacks use the portable client's `$scalarCodecs` constructor
argument. Configure that argument with PHP service configuration or a compiler
pass when callbacks are needed. Null and missing values bypass callbacks.

Subscriptions and incremental delivery are not enabled by this Symfony generator.
Use the separate PHP SDK generator for its native streaming transports.
